; TPS_SWCT_01115 - invalidationPolicy
; Structural semantics:
; - Each INVALIDATION-POLICY must reference exactly one VARIABLE-DATA-PROTOTYPE.
; - HANDLE-INVALID is optional; if present, it has a single value (modeled by function).

(assert
  (forall ((p INVALIDATION-POLICY))
    (has_dataElementRef p)))

; TPS_SWCT_01118 - ClientServerInterface
; A CLIENT-SERVER-OPERATION cannot be reused in the context of a different
; CLIENT-SERVER-INTERFACE. This is modeled by a total function belongsToInterface,
; which makes the interface association functional (i.e., at most one interface).

; No additional axiom is needed beyond the function; reuse would require
; mapping the same operation instance to multiple interfaces, which the
; mapping layer must avoid.

; TPS_SWCT_01119 - Direction of ArgumentDataPrototypes
; Each ArgumentDataPrototype must have a direction.

(assert
  (forall ((a ARGUMENT-DATA-PROTOTYPE))
    (has_direction a)))

; TPS_SWCT_01121 - Pass correct data type
; If an ArgumentDataPrototype is used for in or inout, it must have a typeRef
; to an AUTOSAR-DATA-TYPE of the allowed categories.
; Here we only encode the static part: if it has a typeRef, the referenced
; type must be in one of the allowed categories.

(assert
  (forall ((a ARGUMENT-DATA-PROTOTYPE))
    (=> (has_typeRef a)
        (or (isApplicationArrayDataType (typeRef a))
            (isApplicationCompositeDataType (typeRef a))
            (isApplicationDataType (typeRef a))
            (isApplicationPrimitiveDataType (typeRef a))
            (isApplicationRecordDataType (typeRef a))
            (isImplementationDataType (typeRef a))))))

