; If the association is missing, the object can be placed anywhere
; (default behavior) – this is a semantic property of the generator
; and not directly checkable here. We only encode that if the
; association exists, it is well-formed (already implicit in typing),
; and we introduce a predicate for “conflicting requests” that
; external tooling can assert when mapping multiple component types.

; If there are conflicting requests, this is an error.
(assert
  (not conflictingSwAddrMethodRequests))

; Note: A more detailed model could introduce:
;  - a Sort for the “placed object” (e.g. VARIABLE)
;  - a relation from SW-DATA-DEF-PROPS-CONTENT to that object
;  - and then express that all SwDataDefProps for the same object
;    must agree on the SwAddrMethod. This is left to the environment.

